      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Given a right triangle with sides of lengths 6 cm and 8 cm, and a right angle, we need to find the length of the remaining side. Let's denote the sides of the triangle as \\(a = 6\\) cm, \\(b = 8\\) cm, and the hypotenuse as \\(c\\). According to the Pythagorean theorem, the relationship between the sides of a right triangle is given by:\n\n\\[\na^2 + b^2 = c^2\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\):\n\n\\[\n6^2 + 8^2 = c^2\n\\]\n\nCalculating the squares:\n\n\\[\n36 + 64 = c^2\n\\]\n\n\\[\n100 = c^2\n\\]\n\nTo find \\(c\\), we take the square root of both sides:\n\n\\[\nc = \\sqrt{100}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nc = 10\n\\]\n\nThus, the length of the remaining side of the triangle is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{10.00}\n\\]",
